# Deploy

Use this runbook only for deployment-capable runtimes. Deployment is a state-changing operation and requires explicit target confirmation.

## Required Rules

- Resolve and confirm the approved commit.
- Run local validation before packaging.
- Package committed files only.
- Preserve remote runtime state and secrets.
- Do not delete remote local files unless explicitly instructed.
- Back up before replacing files.
- Restart only confirmed services.
- Run post-deploy health checks.
- Stop on first failed command.
- Report validation and health-check results.

## Inputs

```text
DEPLOY_REF="<branch, tag, or commit>"
REMOTE_USER="<ssh user>"
REMOTE_HOST="<host>"
REMOTE_APP_DIR="<absolute app path>"
SERVICES_TO_RESTART="<space-separated service names>"
```

## Flow

```bash
git status --short
git rev-parse --verify "$DEPLOY_REF"
git log -1 --oneline "$DEPLOY_REF"
make validate
```

Package only committed files from the approved ref, copy to the remote host, take a timestamped backup, replace app files while preserving runtime state, restart confirmed services, and run health checks.
